---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
const updated = '2026-10-06';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy of PlantCare101: No Cookies, Data and Rights" description="Privacy policy of PlantCare101: plant tool inputs stay in your browser, no cookies, no visitor records, a cookieless Clarity stability check and your rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>What the tools do not collect</h2>
    <p>The tools run entirely in your browser. The plant, pot size, light, season and other values you enter, and the plant names you search in the pet-safe checker, are not sent to our servers and are not stored anywhere; in the Microsoft Clarity stability check described below, what you type is masked. There is no account, no newsletter and no form. If you use the share link of the watering calculator, your inputs are written into the page address: only the people you send it to can see them, but the address of a page opened from that link can appear in the Clarity check described below.</p>
    <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted by {LEGAL.hosting.name}. Like any web server, the host records technical data for each request, such as the IP address, the page requested, the date and the browser type, to deliver the site and protect it against abuse. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not use these logs to identify visitors.</p>
    <h2>No cookies, nothing recorded by the publisher</h2>
    <p>PlantCare101 sets no cookie and keeps nothing on your device. The publisher records no personal data about visitors and runs no audience measurement.</p>
    <h2>Stability check: Microsoft Clarity, cookieless</h2>
    <p>Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland) is loaded in cookieless mode: storage is refused before its script starts, so no cookie is set (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), each page view has its own identifier and visits are not linked. Purpose: spotting script errors, slow pages, dead clicks and scrolling problems in the plant guides and tools. Page text and entries are masked in the browser. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a working site (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Retention: 30 days for recordings, 13 months for aggregated figures. Details on the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>.</p>
    <h2>How to object</h2>
    <p>Block the clarity.ms domain in your browser or a content blocker, or write to us. The site stays fully usable. The site shows no advertising.</p>
    <h2>Recipients and processors</h2>
    <p>No data is sold, rented or shared for advertising. The following act as processors under Article 28 GDPR: the host, {LEGAL.hosting.name}, and Microsoft (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited and Microsoft Corporation) for Clarity.</p>
    <h2>Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>The host and Microsoft Corporation are based in the United States and certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework; transfers are also covered by the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses. See <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>. Blocking clarity.ms avoids the Clarity transfer.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Since the publisher is established in the European Union, the General Data Protection Regulation gives you rights of access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability over personal data concerning you. If you write to us, we keep your email only as long as needed to answer. For any request, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You may also complain to the French supervisory authority, the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
    <p>Last updated: {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
